---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import CodeBlock from "../../components/CodeBlock.astro";
import {
  PageHeaderPlayground,
  PageHeaderExamples,
  PageHeaderFocus,
  PageHeaderChrome,
} from "../../components/PageHeaderDemo";
---

<Docs title="Page Header">
  <h1 class="docs-title">Page Header</h1>
  <p class="docs-lead">
    The title, description, and main actions at the top of a page. Inside an app
    shell it moves its title and actions into the shared header bar.
  </p>
  <div class="mt-8"><PageHeaderPlayground client:load /></div>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Usage</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Page header usage"
      code={`import { PageHeader } from "@tulipfarm/sprout/page-header";

<PageHeader
  title="Files"
  description="Find, open, and organize workspace files."
  actions={<>
    <Button><Upload aria-hidden="true" />Upload</Button>
    <Button variant="outline"><FolderAdd aria-hidden="true" />New folder</Button>
  </>}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>title</code> renders the page's only <code>h1</code>. The <code
        >description</code
      > sits under it. The <code>actions</code> sit at the end of the row and wrap
      under the title when space runs out. Long titles wrap; they never overflow.
    </p>
    <PageHeaderExamples client:load />
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Back link and breadcrumb</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Navigation"
      code={`<PageHeader
  title="Customer accounts"
  parent={{ label: "Tables", link: <Link to="/tables" /> }}
/>

<PageHeader
  title="Import skill"
  back={{ label: "Back to skills", link: <Link to="/skills" /> }}
/>`}
    />
    <p>
      <code>back</code> adds a small ghost link above the title. Below 640px only
      its chevron shows; the label stays its accessible name. A <code
        >parent</code
      > shows the title as the last step of a breadcrumb. Both take your router's
      link element, so links stay real links.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Moving focus to the title</h2>
    <p>
      Set <code>focusable</code> to let code focus the heading, for example after
      a route change or after an action removes the focused control. Use <code
        >titleRef</code
      > to reach it and <code>titleId</code> to label a region with it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><PageHeaderFocus client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">App header</h2>
    <CodeBlock
      lang="tsx"
      title="Provide header slots"
      code={`const [title, setTitle] = useState<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);
const [actions, setActions] = useState<HTMLDivElement | null>(null);
const chrome = useMemo(
  () => ({ title, actions, documentTitle: (page) => \`\${page} · Northwind\` }),
  [title, actions],
);

<header>
  <SidebarTrigger />
  <div ref={setTitle} className="flex min-w-0 flex-1 items-center gap-2" />
  <div ref={setActions} className="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-2" />
</header>
<PageChromeContext value={chrome}>
  <Outlet />
</PageChromeContext>`}
    />
    <p>
      When <code>PageChromeContext</code> has both elements, the back link and title
      move into the header bar at 14px and truncate on one line. Actions move beside
      them. The description stays in the page. Pages without a header use <code
        >PageActions</code
      > to place actions there, or right-aligned in the page when there is no header
      bar.
    </p>
    <p>
      <code>documentTitle</code> is optional. When set, a string title also updates
      the browser tab and restores it when the page leaves.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6"><PageHeaderChrome client:load /></div>
  </section>
  <section class="prose-section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Accessibility</h2>
    <p>
      The title is an <code>h1</code>. The breadcrumb is a <code>nav</code> named
      “Breadcrumb”, its last step marked <code>aria-current="page"</code>, and
      its chevrons are hidden from assistive technology. A focusable title shows
      a focus ring only for keyboard focus. Link colors change over 120ms;
      reduced motion turns this off. Routing, dialogs, and menus in these
      examples are sample code.
    </p>
  </section>
</Docs>
